# Each turn calls what nobody knows, which may run anything. It cannot put a variable back into its dead zone, so both are asked in front of the loop, and no turn of the typed copy checks.
# `step` is a constant: what was found in front is what every turn finds, and no turn reads it. `steps` is written by the turns, and by whatever they call for all that the walk knows: it is read in each turn, without a check.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK: frequency=Rare isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = CheckInitialized {{*}}name="step"
# CHECK: = CheckInitialized {{*}}name="steps"
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK: = GetModuleVariable {{*}}followsItsStore
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 0 -1 0 42 13
